Error [jet.InvalidMapKeyType]: `Float` can't be a map key type
  --> tests/ui/map_key_composite_rejected.jet:3:14
    |
  3 |     floats: [Float:Int]{}
    |              ^^^^^
 Why: Map keys must be Int, String, Bool, Char, U8/IntN, a payload-free enum, a list, tuple or struct whose parts recursively follow these rules, or a `KeyBy` type whose key does; Float, views, Shared, functions, maps, sets, and payload-carrying enums are not key-eligible
 Fix: Use an eligible scalar, enum, list, tuple, or struct key, or implement `KeyBy` to name the key; remove non-key fields or store the value separately
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0502

